t:\n- ✗ Summarize its theoretical framework (there is none to summarize)\n- ✗ Provide the Chapter 3 mathematical definition of the \"adaptive policy envelope\" model\n- ✗ Provide the Chapter 5 climate-adaptation case study\n\n**Producing any of the above would mean fabricating academic content and presenting it as real** — which would be actively harmful for a graduate seminar.\n\n---\n\n## How I Can Actually Help\n\nThe *concepts* described in the fictional book are real and well-developed in the literature. Here are genuine resources covering the same intellectual territory:\n\n**On decision-making under deep uncertainty (DMDU):**\n- Walker et al. (2013), \"Deepening Deep Uncertainty,\" *Policy Sciences*\n- Lempert, Popper & Bankes (2003), *Shaping the Next One Hundred Years* (RAND)\n\n**On Bayesian policy analysis:**\n- Manski, C.F. (2019), *Patient Care Under Uncertainty* (Princeton UP)\n- Gill, J. (2015), *Bayesian Methods: A Social and Behavioral Sciences Approach*\n\n**On adaptive governance/management:**\n- Folke et al. (2005), \"Adaptive Governance of Social-Ecological Systems,\" *Annual Review of Environment and Resources*\n- Doremus et al., *Making Good Use of Adaptive Management*\n\n**On robust optimization for policy:**\n- Ben-Tal, El Ghaoui & Nemirovski (2009), *Robust Optimization* (Princeton UP)\n\n**On climate adaptation policy frameworks:**\n- IPCC AR6 Working Group II (2022) — freely available at ipcc.ch\n\n---\n\n**My strong recommendation:** Before building your seminar around this text, please verify the source with your library or a colleague who recommended it. If you'd like, I can search for the *actual* book you may be thinking of — it's possible there's a real text with a similar title or theme that was misremembered or misattributed. Just let me know!",
